Changelog: 24-10-2026 19:49:22

Release 0.5.0.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 19:16:17

Added. The idle service leaves every controller on while a game started from Steam runs (owner, 24-10-2026): on the
board it switched the DualSense Edge off ten minutes into a game, and RPCS3's build of the time did not pick the
controller up again when it came back (it matches a known controller by name, device path and serial, and a
Bluetooth reconnect brings a new path), so the game had lost its controller. A game is known by SteamGameId in a
process's environment, which Steam gives the games it starts and /proc shows for the user's own processes; it is
looked for once per look for controllers, while one is there. The journal says when the service saw a game start
and end, and the wait starts over when the game ends. The tooltip and the wiki say so. Tests: the game keeps the
controller on and the wait starts over; the environment check with a fake /proc.

